    skos:broader rockname:BITCOL ;
    skos:definition "Fusain - A type of bituminous-coal, classified according to lithotype. It is a black, soft, friable coal which closely resembles charcoal. It easily disintegrates into a black, fibrous powder. A hard form of fusain that has been impregnated with mineral matter can be found in some coals. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/03, section 6.1 and fig. 10."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/EarthMaterialClass/RockName> ;
