    skos:broader rockname:MGNCR ;
    skos:definition "Microfoidolitic-rock - A type of medium-grained normal crystalline rock. In the Rock Classification Scheme, it is the medium-grained equivalent of foidolitic-rock. The class includes micronephelinolite. The term may be used as a field classification when an accurate mineral mode from thin section examination is not available. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 5.1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/EarthMaterialClass/RockName> ;
    skos:narrower rockname:MCFDO ;
    skos:notation "MCFDOR"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Microfoidolitic-rock"@en ;
.

