    skos:definition "Meta-igneous rock based on protolith name - In the Rock Classification Scheme, a meta-igneous rock is classified within this category if its igneous protolith is clearly recognisable. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/02, section 5.1 and fig. 1. See also: igneous rock and sediment."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/EarthMaterialClass/RockName> ;
