    skos:broader rockname:PS_SSR ;
    skos:definition "Sedimentary rock based on grain size or crystal size - In the Rock Classification Scheme, if the composition of a sedimentary rock is unknown it may be simply classified by reference to its clast or crystal size. For clastic rocks, the classes are defined in the same way as the siliciclastic sedimentary rocks. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/03, section 10 and fig. 13."@en ;
