    owl:sameAs <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/TUFT> ;
    skos:broader rockname:PCT_VIS ;
    skos:definition "Tuffite - A type of volcaniclastic igneous rock and sediment. In the Rock Classification Scheme, tuffite is a general term for volcaniclastic rocks and sediments which consist of 25 - 75% by volume pyroclastic fragments. The class includes tuffaceous-sedimentary-rock, and tuffaceous-sediment. British Geological Survey Research Report RR/99/06, section 4.2 and figs. 1, 4."@en ;
